<p>In North America, concrete apartment blocks similar to these are reserved for 'subsidised housing' and ghettos.  Not so here in Gimhae, Korea - everybody lives in these.</p>

<p>This suburb of Pusan is  actually much more pleasant than it looks once you get down to the ground level.   There are street markets, soccer fields, small parks and children and families playing everywhere.</p>

<p>Apparently 10 years ago, this view would have only taken in farmers fields.</p>
